cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "structure-negative-steering: negative steering of Boltz-2 structure predictions"
abstract: >-
  Negative steering mutates the receptor surface residues a structure
  prediction wrongly places in contact with its binding partner, so the model
  can no longer settle on that interface. Residues of the intended interface
  are protected from mutation, so what the method removes is a competing site
  rather than the intended one. This repository holds the engine, the
  `negsteer` command line interface, and the Nextflow workflow that runs it on
  a cluster. The benchmark against 18 solved NLR integrated-HMA-domain and
  MAX-effector complexes is in negative-steering-analyses.
authors:
  - family-names: Williams
    given-names: Joshua
    email: joshuandwilliams@outlook.com
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/joshuandwilliams/structure-negative-steering"
keywords:
  - protein structure prediction
  - Boltz-2
  - protein-protein interaction
  - NLR
  - negative design
